  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1013447,
    "UIName": "Taipan",
    "Id": "chassisdef_taipan_TPN-90",
    "Name": "Taipan",
    "Details": "The TPN-90 is a contemporaneous variant of the base Taipan developed for integration into Word of Blake C3 network formations. The Streak SRM 2 launcher and its ammunition are removed and replaced with a rear-right-leg-mounted Improved C3 Computer, contributing networked targeting data to allied units while the twin Light PPCs and MASC system remain unchanged from the TPN-89. The trade of independent close-range firepower for formation coordination reflects the Word of Blake's doctrine of combined-arms C3 warfare.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Improved Jammer</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.98</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Left Upper, Right Upper</color>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_taipan_3160"
  },
  "VariantName": "TPN-90",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "QuadMech",
      "mr-resize-0.46"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Scout",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Taipan is a Word of Blake quad design that came out of the Jihad-era Martinson Armaments plant on Terra, built in limited numbers before the Republic of the Sphere shut down production and the design effectively went extinct before 3090. Quadrupedal light mechs are already a niche category, and the MASC system pushing this one past 150 kph makes it genuinely difficult to engage before it has already fired and repositioned. Most of what survived ended up in museums, which makes finding a working example in the field a notable event.",
